        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s8"
      },
      "text": "In both cases, the executable file was a self-extracting execut­ able containing PoisonIvy, a common backdoor Trojan developed by a Chinese speaker.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_24",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s6"
      },
      "text": "This application is freely available from poisonivy-rat.com.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s10"
      },
      "text": "AntiVirus_update_package.7z • acquisition.7z • offer.7z • update_flashplayer10ax.7z •",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_32",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s4"
      },
      "text": "The second file, happiness.txt, contains custom code in binary format that is en­ crypted and used by xxxx.exe.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_33",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s5"
      },
      "text": "The xxxx.exe file copies happiness.txt to C:\\PROGRAM FILES\\common files\\ ODBC\\ODUBC.DLL and to C:\\WIN­ DOWS\\system32\\jql.sys.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_34",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s6"
      },
      "text": "It then loads the contents of the encrypted file and injects it into the explorer.exe and iexplore.exe processes.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_35",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s7"
      },
      "text": "The injected code copies xxxx.exe to %System%\\winsys.exe and connects to the Command and Control (C&C) server on TCP port 80.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_36",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s8"
      },
      "text": "Once the Trojan establishes the server’s authenticity, it expects a variable-size block of binary code that is read from the server straight into the virtual space for iexplore.exe and then executed.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_41",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s3"
      },
      "text": "pr[REMOVED].noip.org 173.252.207.71, 173.252.205.36, 173.252.205.37, 173.252.205.64 antivirus-groups.com 74.82.166.205, 204.74.215.58 domain.rm6.org 216.131.95.22, 222.255.28.27 anti-virus.sytes.net 173.252.205.36, 173.252.205.37, 173.252.205.64",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_42",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "the_nitro_attacks",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s4"
      },
      "text": "Command and Control (C&C) When executed, the Poison Ivy threat, or Backdoor.Odivy, connects to a command and control (C&C) server over TCP port 80.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
